    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "JAPAN\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktailo\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum\nPremium Beer\nMenus\nApéritif\nJus de Fruit Frais\nFresh orange juice\nOmelette à la Portuguaise\nDelicate omelet with a tangy tomato filling\nDarne de Saumon au Champagne\nAlaskan salmon poached in Champagne\nMignon de Boeuf Grillé\nGrilled filet steak\nLégumes au Beurre\nButtered vegetable bouquet\nPetits Pains\nBreakfast rolls\nCafé\nCoffee\nCafé Décafféiné\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nRiz Pilaf\nPilaf rice\nBeurre et Confitures\nCreamery butter and preserves\nThé\nTea",
      "Légumes au Beurre\nButtered vegetable bouquet\nPetits Pains\nBreakfast rolis\nCate\nCoffee\nCafé Décafféiné\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nRiz Pilaf\nPilaf rice\nBeurre et Confitures\nCreamery butter and preserves\nThé\nTea\nSelected Red and White Wines\nChampagne Brut\nDrambuie Bénédictine Crème de Menthe\nCognac Napoléon Cointreau Kahlúa\nAmaretto di Saronno\n109.K005",
      "JAPAN\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nJAPAN is a land of contrasts. It can display the most neon-lit, skyscrapered and expressway-lined\nface, yet finds its inspiration in the quiet beauty of the graceful Tori Gate and Mt. Fuji, pictured here\nhe Japanese can run their trains at lightening speed, vet spend hours on a small conversationa\ncourtesy. Here you will find graceful perfection and formality contrasted with vigorous commerce\nAmong the many stylish hotels in the capital city of Tokyo is the Keio Plaza Inter-Continental.\nPan Am serves Tokyo on its Round-The-World flights and nonstop daily from New York, San Francisco\nLos Angeles, Honolulu, and Hong Kong. Osaka is served nonstop from Honolulu.\nPAN AM\n2001.080.257"
    ],
